d 'IHSRETRAN': module to compute marginal effects on the original scale for linear regression with an inverse hyperbolic sine (IHS) transformed dependent variable using Duan's smearing estimate.
d
d  ihsretran calculates consistent marginal effects on the original
d scale of the outcome	  variable after estimating a linear
d regression where the dependent variable has been    transformed
d using the inverse hyperbolic sine function [asinh()].    The
d command implements Duan's (1983) nonparametric smearing estimate
d to handle the    retransformation problem from the logarithmic
d components of the hyperbolic sine function,	 as detailed by
d Edward C. Norton (2022). This allows researchers to accurately
d interpret    marginal effects when the dependent variable
d contains zeros or negative values and    exhibits a right-skewed
d distribution. 
d
d KW: marginal efgfects
d KW: retransformation
d KW: regression
d KW: Duan
d
d Requires: Stata version 14
d
d Distribution-Date: 20260921
d
d Author:  Dereje Fedasa,   Dire Dawa University, Ethiopia
d Support: email derejefedasaa@@gmail.com
d
f ihsretran.ado
f ihsretran.sthlp
